MeshBoolean has no coincident-face handling, and coincident faces are the ENTIRE content of a self-boolean. `FaceBoundary` is declared at `apps/spark/MeshBoolean.codex:17` and is never constructed anywhere in the tree, and `csg-point-inside` answers only FaceInside or FaceOutside from ray-crossing parity, which for a face centroid lying exactly ON the tool's surface is arbitrary; `csg-keep-a`/`csg-keep-b` have no FaceBoundary arm either. Measured: self-union yields 24 verts where A union A = A is 36, and self-difference yields 36 where A minus A is 0. The compile path (act-form opening) and float-equality (det ~0, CDX2085) are fixed here and the primitive path is pinned by spark-mesh-test. Un-skip when MeshBoolean classifies coincident faces and both keep functions carry a FaceBoundary arm.